     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Manuel,<div><br></div><div>This would be a cool development. But it would take a lot of work. In theory, any model that can be implemented in Stan can also be implemented in brms or other Stan-wrapping packages. There is a nice repo here <a href=\"https://github.com/stan-dev/example-models/tree/master/BPA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/stan-dev/example-models/tree/master/BPA&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494567092000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0xXkvEOJwgw4b6C23hpwR3\">https://github.com/stan-dev/example-models/tree/master/BPA</a> that has Stan code for several of the hierarchical models you are referring to. The hard part would be creating a class of brms functions that convert a wide variety of occupancy or n-mixture models from standard R syntax to Stan syntax. Same goes for data structures.  It would be great if the brms functions handled model statements and data structures consistent with unmarked functions. Whoever created such functions would provide a huge contribution to the quantitative ecology community.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Tim</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Wed, May 8, 2019 at 11:17 PM &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hmec...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211);max-width:850px;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n  <div style=\"background-color:rgb(245,245,245);padding:10px 20px\">\r\n    <table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%\">\r\n      <tbody>\r\n        <tr>\r\n          <td style=\"width:70%\">\r\n            <span style=\"font:18px/20px arial;color:rgb(51,51,51)\">\r\n              <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/hmecology/topics\" style=\"text-decoration:none;color:rgb(51,51,51)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/hmecology/topics&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494567092000&amp;usg=AOvVaw23YGjSnSjWSEGGc0A5rchv\">\r\n              hmec...@googlegroups.com</a>\r\n            </span>\r\n          </td>\r\n          <td style=\"text-align:right;width:30%\">\r\n            <span style=\"font:20px/24px arial\"><a style=\"color:rgb(221,75,57);text-decoration:none\" href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email/#!overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail/%23!overview&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494567092000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3R4BtVqoybcnQRUrVgKN2H\">Google Groups</a></span>\r\n          </td>\r\n          <td style=\"width:32px\">\r\n            <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email/#!overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail/%23!overview&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494567092000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3R4BtVqoybcnQRUrVgKN2H\"><img style=\"border:0px;vertical-align:middle\" src=\"https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/4SGWHe9midrWMDxDIJMQraTMMgnAU71soPZ0D28IOSZcs66TdyRoCqyIhaTt-kwo0YKv2lRo05RkwsGFZdnFhdvy60XdxNlL2U-B=s0-d-e1-ft#http://www.google.com/images/icons/product/groups-32.png\"></a>\r\n          </td>\r\n        </tr>\r\n      </tbody>\r\n    </table>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <div style=\"padding:20px;background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\">\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"font-family:arial;color:rgb(34,34,34);padding:0px\">\r\n  <a name=\"m_-8660604610562110975_m_3135310446690499404_digest_top\" style=\"font-size:21px\" rel=\"nofollow\">\r\n  \r\n  \r\n    Topic digest\r\n  \r\n  </a><br>\r\n  <span style=\"font-size:11px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/hmecology/topics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/hmecology/topics&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494567092000&amp;usg=AOvVaw23YGjSnSjWSEGGc0A5rchv\">View all topics</a>\r\n  </span>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font:13px/18px arial;color:rgb(34,34,34);padding:0px;margin-bottom:30px\">\r\n  <ul style=\"margin-left:3px;padding-left:0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <li>\r\n      <a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_-8660604610562110975_m_3135310446690499404_group_thread_0\" rel=\"nofollow\">\r\n      Fitting hierarchical models with the R package brms</a> -\r\n      <span style=\"color:rgb(119,119,119)\">2 Updates</span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  \r\n  </ul>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_-8660604610562110975_m_3135310446690499404_group_thread_0\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0px 5px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/hmecology/t/3bd2c91e1a0a341d?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/hmecology/t/3bd2c91e1a0a341d?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494567092000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Sp9kIzWKrrElLfiopG5vA\">\r\n      Fitting hierarchical models with the R package brms\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n      <tbody><tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n          &quot;Manuel Spínola&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mspin...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: May 08 07:44AM -0600\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        Dear list members,<br>\r\n <br>\r\nI was wondering whether it would be possible to fit occupancy models (or<br>\r\nother hierarchical models) with the R package brms.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nThe brms package fit Bayesian generalized (non-)linear multivariate<br>\r\nmultilevel models using &#39;Stan&#39; for full Bayesian inference, and is very<br>\r\nflexible very well supported in the R community.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nDoes anybody in the list have an insight on this?<br>\r\n <br>\r\nThank you very much in advance.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nManuel<br>\r\n <br>\r\n-- <br>\r\n*Manuel Spínola, Ph.D.*<br>\r\nInstituto Internacional en Conservación y Manejo de Vida Silvestre<br>\r\nUniversidad Nacional<br>\r\nApartado 1350-3000<br>\r\nHeredia<br>\r\nCOSTA RICA<br>\r\n<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mspi...@una.cr</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mspi...@una.ac.cr</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mspin...@gmail.com</a><br>\r\nTeléfono: (506) 8706 - 4662<br>\r\nPersonal website: Lobito de río &lt;<a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/lobitoderio/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://sites.google.com/site/lobitoderio/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494567092000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1JW5GOTWuuY9NX3c7JyXxq\">https://sites.google.com/site/lobitoderio/</a>&gt;<br>\r\nInstitutional website: ICOMVIS &lt;<a href=\"http://www.icomvis.una.ac.cr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.icomvis.una.ac.cr/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494567092000&amp;usg=AOvVaw27DHx4da09IAEsN0wdQtuR\">http://www.icomvis.una.ac.cr/</a>&gt;<br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n      <tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n          Jarrett Byrnes &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jarrett...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: May 08 09:45AM -0400\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        You can fit zero inflation with these models, so you should be able to do so. Would be great to see some examples. <br>\r\n <br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </tbody></table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_-8660604610562110975_m_3135310446690499404_digest_top\" rel=\"nofollow\">Back to top</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  </div>\r\n  <div style=\"background-color:rgb(245,245,245);padding:5px 20px\">\r\n  <table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%\">\r\n  <tbody><tr>\r\n    <td style=\"padding-top:4px;font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(99,99,99);font-size:11px\">\r\n      \r\n      You received this digest because you&#39;re subscribed to updates for this group. You can change your settings on the <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/hmecology/join\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/hmecology/join&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494567092000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3B1BXpMppRW67c6REhZmGf\">group membership page</a>.<br>\r\n      To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hmecology+...@googl